        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Imperialism</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Period</span><span class="info-stat-val">c. 1870 CE – present</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Thinkers</span><span class="info-stat-val">its advocates Joseph Chamberlain, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cecil-rhodes">Cecil Rhodes</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jules-ferry">Jules Ferry</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/evelyn-baring-1st-earl-of-cromer">Lord Cromer</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-curzon">Lord Curzon</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alfred-milner">Lord Milner</a> and the writer Rudyard Kipling; the political geographers Friedrich Ratzel and Halford Mackinder; its theorists and critics John A. Hobson, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladimir-lenin">Vladimir Lenin</a>, Joseph Schumpeter, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/walter-rodney">Walter Rodney</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-said">Edward Said</a></span></div>
